  title: [Judge the contents, not the box],
  author: [Derek Sivers],
  source-name: [Derek Sivers],
  images: (),
  paragraphs: (
  [My cousin took a course on a complete system for physical fitness and health, and followed every bit of its advice.
She had great results at first.
But then she saw the coach’s social media posts, and hated his political beliefs, so now she doesn’t follow that course at all.],
  [A best-selling book on psychology is filled with wisdom that would improve your life, if applied.
But a few sentences were found to be plagiarized, or some of its studies don’t replicate.
So people trash the whole book and refuse to read it.],
  [That’s the problem with judging a box instead of its contents.
It’s seeking “true” instead of useful.
